WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:01.189 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  a rare sound in afghanistan  [Music]  a musician and driver akhtar has lived  in a refugee camp since his childhood  he's among the more than three million  people displaced in afghanistan  before it was good but now life just  passes us by before we could find some  food for our children but the change in  government means there is no work now a  year ago tens of thousands of people  headed for the borders as provinces fell  to the taliban  many in kabul rushed to the airport as  the western-backed government collapsed  after taking refuge abroad ashraf  ghani's denied that he escaped with  suitcases full of cash  more than a hundred thousand people left  during the abrupt withdrawal of foreign  forces  the economy collapsed and the u.s rose  billions of dollars of foreign reserves  the u.s nato alliance spent an estimated  300 million dollars a day every day for  two decades but basics such as roads  schools hospitals are either  non-existent or in poor shape since the  taliban took over that money has stopped  coming in  and thousands of professionals have left  human rights watch has accused the  taliban of a long list of abuses  restricting the rights of women and  girls suppressing media freedom and  detaining torturing and executing  critics and perceived opponents  all allegations the taliban denies  in some other areas things are good  we're trying to improve but we should  also take into account the problems of  the coronavirus the suspension of  foreign aid the freezing of money the  problems in banking the drought all of  these together have increased the  problems for the people of afghanistan  for those who've left life's not easy  more than half the 20 000 afghans who  reach the uk are still in temporary  accommodation there's a lack of  prospects abroad and many face  harassment and the threat of detention  i lost everything including my  restaurant i planned to go to europe so  i went to turkey unfortunately they  captured us and deported us to iran  thank god now we are in our homeland and  i will never go anywhere else  in a year security has improved but  poverty and desperation have increased  and while the taliban seeks  international recognition there are some  concessions it seems unwilling to  down to make  [Music]

